// Build settings the app target always has, whether or not this machine has a
// routing key. Referenced from `project.yml`, so it survives
// `xcodegen generate` — a setting typed into Xcode's UI does not.

// **The default is "no key", and that is a working build.** A fresh checkout and
// CI have no `Secrets.xcconfig`, and they must still compile, launch and run
// their tests. No key simply means routing is disabled: legs keep their raw
// geometry and draw dashed (PD-2), which is an existing designed state with
// user-facing copy already written for it — not an error path.
KAMOME_ROUTING_API_KEY =

// The optional include. `#include?` — note the `?` — is not an error when the
// file is absent, which is exactly the fresh-checkout case above. When the file
// does exist it is read after the default, so it wins.
//
// `Config/Secrets.xcconfig` is gitignored and generated locally from
// `~/.kamome/routing.env`; `Config/Secrets.xcconfig.example` is the template.
#include? "Secrets.xcconfig"
